      "name": "OperationObservation",
      "signature": "enum OperationObservation { Absent, Exact(VerifiedExternalEvidence), Conflict(ExternalConflict), Unverifiable(ObservationFailure) }",
      "description": "A closed graph-layer classification returned by observing one graph-private prepared operation against its provider; it preserves absence, exact equality, conflict, and inability to verify as different states.",
      "error_conditions": [
        "Provider authentication, authorization, rate limit, malformed output, unsupported client behavior, timeout, or transport failure produces Unverifiable, never Absent.",
        "An object with the intended name/version but different target, bytes, metadata, or asset roster produces Conflict, never Exact."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "observe_prepared",
      "signature": "observe_prepared(capability: &ValidatedReleaseIntent, operation: &ReleaseOperationId) -> OperationObservation",
      "description": "The single graph-private read boundary used before mutation, after mutation, by execute, and by reconcile for every operation role.",
      "error_conditions": [
        "The operation is not part of the validated intent or lacks an exact prepared provider identity.",
        "The provider cannot prove the operation's role-specific equality contract."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "converge_release",
      "signature": "converge_release(capability, artifact_manifest, state_store, receipt_store, permit) -> ReleaseReceipt",
      "description": "Observes the canonical DAG in order, mutates only Absent operations with satisfied observed prerequisites, re-observes postconditions, persists diagnostic state atomically, and returns only after a complete receipt is persisted.",
      "error_conditions": [
        "Any operation is Conflict or Unverifiable.",
        "An Absent operation remains non-Exact after its single effect attempt.",
        "Any prerequisite is not Exact in the current convergence pass.",
        "State or receipt persistence fails."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "reconcile_release",
      "signature": "reconcile_release(capability, artifact_manifest, optional_state) -> ReleaseObservationReport",
      "description": "Performs the same complete external observation pass as execution without ApplyPermit or mutation and reports every exact, absent, conflicting, or unverifiable operation.",
      "error_conditions": [
        "Intent, source, artifact, or prepared-input validation fails before provider observation.",
        "The report cannot cover every operation exactly once."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-001",
      "criterion": "Every operation role has one production observer that returns exactly Absent, Exact with safe typed evidence, Conflict with a closed reason, or Unverifiable with an actionable transient diagnostic. Execute, reconcile, pre-effect checks, post-effect checks, and interruption recovery call that same observer rather than reconstructing provider semantics in sibling paths.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-002",
      "criterion": "Execution observes every operation in canonical DAG order regardless of whether the optional journal says Pending, Attempting, Published, AlreadySatisfied, Failed, or Blocked. Exact is recorded as satisfied without mutation; Absent is mutated at most once in that invocation and must be Exact on post-effect observation; Conflict or Unverifiable exits nonzero without mutating that operation or any dependent operation.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-003",
      "criterion": "A missing, unreadable, stale, or entirely lost execution-state file cannot widen authority or prevent recovery. A fresh runner given the same immutable intent and artifact manifest observes exact existing objects, skips their mutation, creates only absent objects, and converges to the same result; state remains an atomically persisted diagnostic journal bound to the intent.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-004",
      "criterion": "Release execute returns exit status zero only after every intended operation is observed Exact in the same final pass and a matching ReleaseReceipt is atomically persisted. Any Pending, Attempting, Failed, Blocked, Absent, Conflict, Unverifiable, missing operation, missing receipt, or receipt-write failure exits nonzero and names the incomplete operation and recovery action.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-005",
      "criterion": "A receipt records the intent digest, exact operation roster, observation time-independent safe evidence identities and digests, and whether each object was newly produced or already present. It is output evidence only: execute and reconcile re-observe providers on every invocation and never accept receipt bytes as proof that an external object still exists or still matches.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-006",
      "criterion": "Registry observation compares the provider's immutable published artifact set with the matching expected RegistryPackage entries in the intent-bound artifact manifest: crates.io-compatible publication verifies the .crate checksum, npm verifies the packed tarball integrity or bytes, and PyPI verifies the complete expected distribution-file name and SHA-256 set. A present exact set is prominently reported and never republished; missing is publishable; a partial set, different digest, extra conflicting distribution, or provider response that cannot prove equality is fatal.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-007",
      "criterion": "Remote tag observation queries the configured remote rather than local refs and proves the exact tag name resolves to the intended source commit and required annotated-tag content. A matching local-only tag is neither Exact nor post-push confirmation; a conflicting remote tag is fatal; after creation or push, the remote is re-observed before any forge-release or asset operation becomes eligible.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-008",
      "criterion": "GitHub Release observation uses supported GitHub CLI or API arguments, classifies the real nonzero-exit HTTP 404 contract as Absent, preserves 401, 403, 429, 5xx, malformed, and transport results as Unverifiable, and proves release identity through the separately verified remote tag rather than target_commitish. Exactness also covers the required draft/prerelease policy and final asset roster.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-009",
      "criterion": "GitHub asset observation addresses the exact ProductReleaseId and slot file name, downloads or queries immutable digest-capable data, and proves byte length and SHA-256 against the artifact manifest. An existing same-name asset with a different or unverifiable digest is fatal and is never overwritten; after an upload, the asset is re-observed as Exact before completion.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-010",
      "criterion": "Release reconcile is structurally read-only and emits a complete report for every operation, not merely a list of locally eligible Pending entries. It requires no ApplyPermit, invokes no registry publish, Git push, GitHub creation, or upload route, and exits nonzero when the intended release is not completely Exact while preserving the full observation report in JSON output.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-011",
      "criterion": "Boundary tests exercise realistic subprocess contracts: real Git with a bare remote for absent, exact, and conflicting tags; argv parsing compatible with the installed gh CLI; gh HTTP 404 with its real nonzero exit; 401, 403, 429, and 5xx failures; and local HTTP registry fixtures for absent, exact, conflicting, and unverifiable artifact metadata. An argv-insensitive fake or exit-zero 404 alone cannot satisfy this criterion.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-012",
      "criterion": "An interruption test stops at each boundary between attempt persistence, provider mutation, provider success, post-effect observation, terminal-state persistence, and receipt persistence, then resumes with both the same journal and no journal on a fresh runner. Every case either converges without repeating an Exact effect or exits nonzero for Conflict/Unverifiable; no case can return successful incomplete state.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-013",
      "criterion": "The graph-private prepared operation remains the only effect and observation input. Provider adapters cannot accept free-form package, version, endpoint, tag, repository, asset name, or digest values from CLI flags, workflow environment, mutable configuration, or execution state after the intent has been validated.",
      "is_error_case": true
    }
  ],
